-- chem/magloop.hypercubical — the U(1) loops of Thiemann's magnetic operator acting on the labels at a vertex, and the flux
-- between vertices conserved by every term of it. At a vertex v the edges' ends are EdgeEnds (chem/magnetic.hypercubical): the
-- innermost segment label and the labels outward, the last being the label of the edge beyond every arc. The loop
-- α_jk = s_j ∘ a_jk ∘ s_k⁻¹ raised to the power s (= ±1) pushes a new innermost segment on end j with its label
-- shifted by s and on end k shifted by −s. A word is a product of such loops; the U(1) factor of the magnetic
-- operator is a sum of words with rational coefficients, S_α S_β = −¼(h_α h_β − h_α h_β⁻¹ − h_α⁻¹ h_β + h_α⁻¹ h_β⁻¹).
-- Proved: every word, so every term of every such sum, leaves the labels beyond every arc unchanged (`word-keeps`).
-- The fiber of the observation `beyonds` (the flux each edge carries between its vertices) is closed under the
-- operator: it acts within each fiber, which is the sector decomposition, a statement here and not an argument.
import "magnetic.hypercubical"

